mputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨2,3,-3⟩-⟨5,9,-6⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,-6,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨3,2,7⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-3)\\cdot 3+(-6)\\cdot 2+3\\cdot 7|}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{7}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-9-12+21|}{\\sqrt{9+4+49}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,0\\,|}{\\sqrt{62}} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $P$ lies on the plane."] [17592186120250 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] [17592186117659 :answer-field/correct 17592186117662] ["activity-efa2f5ef-e6fe-56c3-a086-47568aefef07" :activity/id #uuid "efa2f5ef-e6fe-56c3-a086-47568aefef07"] ["step-4ebaacee-c917-59e0-9efc-2e133291f49e" :step/id #uuid "4ebaacee-c917-59e0-9efc-2e133291f49e"] ["step-8c864f64-ba38-5a69-aef8-6cd249fd9aa2" :step/id #uuid "8c864f64-ba38-5a69-aef8-6cd249fd9aa2"] ["step-f2cfe04d-a967-51d9-b573-04f9a99a2b6e" :step/id #uuid "f2cfe04d-a967-51d9-b573-04f9a99a2b6e"] ["step-de00c837-e9c3-5a67-b184-8bf559752fe5" :step/id #uuid "de00c837-e9c3-5a67-b184-8bf559752fe5"] ["step-d1bf76c1-13f5-53ce-b624-03ea4de1d4f3" :step/id #uuid "d1bf76c1-13f5-53ce-b624-03ea4de1d4f3"] ["step-4ebaacee-c917-59e0-9efc-2e133291f49e" :step/content 17592186120250] ["step-4ebaacee-c917-59e0-9efc-2e133291f49e" :step/next "step-8c864f64-ba38-5a69-aef8-6cd249fd9aa2"] ["step-8c864f64-ba38-5a69-aef8-6cd249fd9aa2" :step/content 17592186120295] ["step-8c864f64-ba38-5a69-aef8-6cd249fd9aa2" :step/next "step-f2cfe04d-a967-51d9-b573-04f9a99a2b6e"] ["step-f2cfe04d-a967-51d9-b573-04f9a99a2b6e" 